# Keep the build context small.
#
# Without this Docker uploads the entire working tree to the daemon before the build even
# starts — .venv, .toolchain, the downloaded archive data and node_modules come to about
# 1.4 GB, none of which the build uses. On Windows, where the context crosses the WSL2
# file-sharing boundary, that upload dominates the build time.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets must never enter the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Recreated inside the image.
.venv
.toolchain
**/node_modules
web/dist
services/gateway/bin

# Downloaded at first start, or baked in by the build itself.
data

# Caches and build litter.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.DS_Store

# Not used by any build stage.
docs
deploy/oracle
scripts
infra
*.md
LICENSE
Makefile
